<SubpageLayout
  title="Making Your System Legible to AI Agents"
  description="Chapter 6 of The Day After AI: Making Your System Legible to AI Agents. The technical model for agent-navigable architecture."
  section="chapters"
  crumbLabel="Ch.6: Making Your System Legible to AI Agents"
>
  <h1>Making Your System Legible to AI Agents</h1>
  <p class="lede">The technical model for agent-navigable architecture</p>

  <p>
    Chapter 6 is the technical model for a system an agent can navigate.
    It covers what agents actually need. It covers contract completeness:
    the minimum viable contract, the extended contract, and anti-patterns.
    It covers MCP as the runtime bridge, the agent onboarding test, and
    governing the graph under agent-assisted evolution.
  </p>
  <p>
    The agent onboarding test checks whether a capability's contract is
    enough, on its own, for an agent to navigate the capability safely.
    It evaluates the contract, not the agent. The book's write-up of that
    test, including scoring bands and a legibility index, is
    <a href={withBase("/appendix/agent-onboarding-test/")}>Appendix C</a>.
  </p>

